(:doc :symbol "asl/agentLoop/context.asl#" :text "Leon's context, vendor bounds, turn signals, possible sites, prefetch, spec check and advisor IO, ported from scripts/agentLoop/loop.py 4433-4760 and 4823-5340 (parity: asl/agentLoop/tests/contextParityTest.asl against tests/parity/agentLoop/contextParityGen.py). Receipts, ops, gate results and served facts are j/Json objects read with Python's get/truthiness/str rules. Model calls take the provider as a function value: a reviewer ask is (intent system user) -> (Result (Option String) String) and an advisor advise is (system user) -> the same, so U1's providers nextTurn!/advise! adapt to either; an err is the provider error's message. External tools (git) run through asl-proc exec! argv; a spawn failure is an err. Strings are bytes; Python's char lengths and cuts are counted in code points; strip follows Python's Unicode whitespace set, while \\s, \\w, isdigit and lower are their ASCII cases, and a file read for prefetch is taken as UTF-8.")
